  "id": "framing-effect",
  "term": "framing effect",
  "definition": "A framing effect is a change in people’s reasoning or opinions caused by how an issue is presented. In this packet, it refers especially to metaphorical framing, where describing an abstract topic through a particular metaphor can activate matching knowledge and lead people toward frame-consistent inferences.",
